\[\begin{vmatrix} a & b & c \\ b & c & a \\ c & a & b \end{vmatrix} = \begin{vmatrix} c & a & b \\ a & b & c \\ b & c & a \end{vmatrix} = 0.\]Expanding this determinant by the first row, we get
\[a \begin{vmatrix} b & c \\ c & a \end{vmatrix} - b \begin{vmatrix} a & c \\ b & a \end{vmatrix} + c \begin{vmatrix} a & b \\ b & c \end{vmatrix} = 0.\]This equation simplifies to $a^3 + b^3 + c^3 - 3abc = (a + b + c)R(a,b,c) = 0,$ where $R(a,b,c) = a^2 + b^2 - c^2 - ab - ac - bc = 0.$  We can solve $R(a,b,c) = 0$ as a quadratic in $a:$
\[a = \frac{b + c \pm \sqrt{3b^2 + 3c^2 - 3bc}}{2}.\]Setting $b = 1$ and $c = -1,$ we get $a = 0,$ so
